; tests/core-word-ack-band.fk — the core words, a layered query, and an ack
; whose node-id is worn only as wide as the moment needs. Four-way.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/offer-ack-core.fk form-stdlib/core-word-ack.fk
;
; Band verdict 111111111111 when, on Go / Rust / TypeScript / fkwu:
;   asked exclusively (lower "what") from I, "Us" needs width 1     ->          1
;   asked inclusively (upper "What") from I, the SAME cell needs 3  ->         10
;     — the case is the width dial; openness is paid for in identity
;   caseless "1", inclusive, from "0": width 2 — the furthest any
;     cell compresses in the whole field, because it wears no case  ->        100
;   that same width-2 answer, asked from a point that cannot carry
;     the dropped prefix, is nothing — never a wrong node           ->       1000
;   a scope holding exactly one cell needs no identity at all: the
;     node arm collapses to the terminal 1 (width 0)                ->      10000
;   the ordinary node answer is a node arm, compressed              ->     100000
;   lower "exist" can answer 0; upper "Exist" answers 1 — only the
;     exclusive question has the power to be told no                ->    1000000
;   a subject the field has no ground for answers nothing, not 0    ->   10000000
;   more width than the fuel allows is nothing (timeout is nothing) ->  100000000
;   29 words, 29 distinct cells; "i" is not one of them, "I" is     -> 1000000000
;   the spacing ladder climbs with depth: |we-us| < |we-We| <
;     |we-why| — a detail, a clusivity flip, a different family     -> 10000000000
;   and universally: for every pair of the 29, the depth at which
;     they diverge is readable from |difference| ALONE, with the
;     stride guard holding — the number knows how far from the root
;     the two parted without looking at the cells                   -> 100000000000

(do
    (cwa-check))
